<title>CANADA: Canadian oilseed crushing data for 1995 vs 1994.</title>
<headline>Canadian oilseed crushing data for 1995 vs 1994.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Oilseed Processors Association detailed Monday the level of oilseed crushing for 1995, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>		1995 OILSEED CRUSHINGS</p>
<p>	     CRUSH 1994   OIL   1994   MEAL   1994</p>
<p>Canola     2,547 2,328  1,072  974   1,596  1,431</p>
<p>Soybeans   1,169 1,046    202  187     908    814</p>
<p>Sunflower     47    50     20   21	17     18</p>
<p>Flaxseed	72    29     25   10	46     18</p>
<p>Meal statistics include additional screening, or dockage, tonnage added on, a COPA official said.</p>
<p>COPA consists of Archer Daniels Midland Co, CanAmera Foods, Canbra Foods Ltd with crush data also provided by  Cargill Ltd, the Canadian unit of Minnesota-based Cargill Inc.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
